    "intro": "The Church of the Holy Trinity at Green Island is the Anglican church serving one of the larger communities on the south coast of Hanover, a fishing and farming town on the sheltered waters of Green Island Harbour. The harbour gave the settlement commercial significance during the plantation era as a loading point for sugar from the surrounding estates, and the community that grew here has maintained a distinctive character shaped by both the sea and the interior agriculture of southern Hanover. Holy Trinity has served as the spiritual anchor for Green Island and the surrounding district for well over a century, providing worship, baptisms, burials, and pastoral care to the coastal community.",
