    "intro": "St. James' Anglican Church serves Kendal, a community in Manchester parish, confirmed by Google Places at coordinates 18.0737, -77.4937. The church serves this interior farming community in the northern part of Manchester. Kendal is a community in the rolling hills of central Manchester, its name drawn from the Kendal in the Lake District of England.",
    "history": "Kendal sits in the interior of Manchester, in the farming landscape of the parish's central hills. The name derives from Kendal in Westmorland (now Cumbria), England — a connection that reflects the pattern of colonial estate proprietors naming their properties after their English home towns. The Anglican Diocese established St. James' to serve this community.",
