    "intro": "St. Paul's Anglican Church serves Mile Gully, a community in the interior of Manchester parish near the famous St. George's Church ruins — known locally as 'Duppy Church.' Mile Gully is a community in the hills of Manchester, and St. Paul's provides active Anglican ministry alongside the historic ruined church that stands as a landmark in the area.",
    "history": "Mile Gully sits in the interior of Manchester, in the hill country of the parish. The proximity to the ruined St. George's Church — abandoned and roofless, with graves dating back centuries — gives Mile Gully a particular historical character. St. Paul's has served as the active Anglican worship point in the community, continuing the tradition of Christian worship in this area long after the old St. George's fell into disuse.",
