    "history": "St. Mary's Chapel was established to serve the Lawrencefield estate and surrounding community in St. Andrew. Its primary initial function was to serve the spiritual needs of the planter family, overseers, and the enslaved population of the estate. Following emancipation in the 1830s, the chapel's role transformed significantly. It became a cornerstone for the newly freed community, providing a formal and enduring space for worship, baptisms, marriages, and funerals, thereby helping to foster a distinct village identity separate from the plantation system. Throughout the 20th century, it persisted as a minor but stable chapelry within the wider Anglican parish structure.",
