    "clergy": "As a mission chapel, Mount James has historically shared clergy with nearby churches in the St. Andrew hills, typically St. Andrew Parish Church, St. Mark’s (Gordon Town), St. Martin (Irish Town), and other mountain congregations. Clergy rotated between outstations for services, confirmations, pastoral visits, and seasonal celebrations. In the diocesan structure, it continues to be part of the St. Andrew region, receiving support from the regional clergy team rather than having its own resident priest.",
    "interestingFacts": "Mount James sits along one of the scenic ridges overlooking the Kingston plain, close to trails and old estate roads leading toward Content Gap and the higher Blue Mountains. The chapel has long served as a landmark for hikers and rural travellers moving between Stony Hill and the upper coffee districts. Because the area is relatively isolated during heavy rains or landslides, the church has often doubled as a local meeting point during community organising or relief efforts.",
