    "history": "St. Thomas Anglican Church was founded in the 18th century when Jamaica was still a slave society. Lacovia was an important inland crossing point on the Black River, and the church served estate owners, free people of color, and some enslaved people who had limited permission to attend. After Emancipation in 1838, many freed people settled near Lacovia for its river and farmland. The church grew quickly during this period and became a strong center for Anglican worship in the region. Throughout the 1800s, St. Thomas played a major role in education, baptisms, marriages, and community life for people rebuilding their lives after slavery.",
