    "intro": "All Souls Anglican Church serves the rural communities of Brompton and Luana, located inland from Black River on St. Elizabeth's south coast. Established to provide local Anglican worship separate from Black River's main parish church, it grew alongside the area's historic estates and farming settlements. The churchyard's tombstones document generations of local families, from estate workers to community leaders. In recent years, the building has expanded its role to include community shelter and meeting space, demonstrating its ongoing significance beyond Sunday worship.",
