    "intro": "All Saints Anglican Church is an old church in the cool hills of Malvern, built in the 1800s as the area grew after Emancipation in 1838. It became a center of worship for families who settled in the mountains and for students at Munro College and Hampton School. The church has survived strong hurricanes, repairs, and many changes from the time of slavery through Jamaica’s Independence in 1962. Today, it remains an important part of the Malvern community and continues to serve both residents and students.",
