    "intro": "St. Mary’s Anglican Church at Montpelier is a historic church in St. James, built in 1847 on a hill overlooking the former Montpelier sugar estate. Its site is deeply layered with history, having been part of an estate attacked during the 1831-32 Baptist War and potentially built on the foundation of a slave hospital. Today, this simple Gothic Revival stone church serves as both an active place of worship and a quiet heritage landmark, symbolizing the transition from a landscape of enslavement to one of community and faith.",
