    "history": "St. Michael’s Anglican Church was established in the late 19th century to serve the growing population of Clarks Town. After Emancipation in 1838, many formerly enslaved families left coastal estates to establish new homes and farms in this inland area. In response, the Anglican Diocese sent clergy to provide religious guidance and community support. By the 1880s, a permanent stone church was completed and dedicated to St. Michael the Archangel, a figure symbolizing strength and justice. It quickly became a central institution for worship, education, and community gatherings, helping to stabilize the new free village.",
